  Auto-identify is a bit powerful, but give them at high level an identify 
spell working as the teleport spell works now, i.e. no spellbook needed.
Then normal spell-casting limitations (i.e. power and food consumption)
will regulate its use. 
  Or another idea: an auto-identify but without bless/curse status, without
magical plusses/minuses and without the number of charges - you have to find 
it by one of the 'traditional' ways, or id by a scroll/spell anyhow. That
would be very easy to implement - once the character is at high enough level 
just mark all rings/wands/amulets/scrolls/potions/spellbooks (but not gems and 
normal armor/weapons) as identified.
  And, maybe it would be good if the wizards had a few extra items 'identified'
from the beginning - after all, they must have learned someting in the
wizard's school, no? Like: you start with e.g. scroll of identify and 
scare monster, but you also have scrolls of enchant weapon and magic mapping
already identified... Same for potions and wands.
